& [BoundaryFormation] separates deterministic reconciliation from physical observation
  + [inside] one exact outer profile, one nonzero caller-owned reconciliation identity, and two strict supplied-entry assembly inputs named pre_read and post_read
  + [inside] independent nested assembly, syntax-identity validation, closed exact field comparison, deterministic first-difference classification, and atomic stable-pair or fault release
  + [outside] query invocation, buffer initialization, actual order, same-handle or same-object proof, clocks, paths, content reads, digests, Git modes, ordinals, directory inventories, traversal, receipts, admission, and effects
  + [input_roles] pre_read and post_read are declaration labels rather than observed temporal facts
  + [output_strength] stable means equal under the exact supplied field comparison profile only

& [AtomicRequirementSet] is complete
  + [M2B-ESR-001] require exact outer profile, strict JSON, preserved source, governing protocol, and both nonoptional nested inputs
  + [M2B-ESR-002] invoke the current supplied-entry assembly validator independently for pre_read and post_read and preserve a nested fault side
  + [M2B-ESR-003] require a nonzero caller-owned reconciliation identity and preserve it without assigning physical meaning
  + [M2B-ESR-004] require nonzero equal entry-reference identities after both assemblies pass
  + [M2B-ESR-005] require nonzero distinct pre-read and post-read batch identities without treating distinctness as order proof
  + [M2B-ESR-006] compare kind, full policy decision, diagnostic reparse tag, strong identity, allocation size, end-of-file, link count, and raw stream records exactly in canonical order
  + [M2B-ESR-007] stop at the first canonical difference and emit one closed difference-field identity
  + [M2B-ESR-008] release exactly one complete stable pair or one bounded typed fault with no partial pair
  + [M2B-ESR-009] preserve both admitted observations, the reconciliation identity, common entry reference, distinct batch identities, and the fixed comparison-field account
  + [M2B-ESR-010] reject unknown outer or nested fields, variants, omissions, wrong types, and malformed input without bypassing nested assembly validation
  + [M2B-ESR-011] state that labels and syntax identities do not prove physical provenance, order, sameness, freshness, supported platform, path binding, content stability, or trust
  + [M2B-ESR-012] preserve zero dependency, unsafe, platform-call, I/O, traversal, receipt, admission, mutation, seal, or promotion delta and bind complete verification

& [DataDesignModel] is one pure composite transform
  + [ReconciliationRequest] is outer profile, reconciliation_identity u64, pre_read AssemblyInput, and post_read AssemblyInput
  + [NestedAssembly] is the existing pure transform applied independently to each nested input
  + [AdmittedPreObservation] is the successful pre_read assembly result
  + [AdmittedPostObservation] is the successful post_read assembly result
  + [SyntaxIdentityGate] checks reconciliation identity, shared entry reference, and distinct batch identities
  + [StabilityComparedField] is the closed ordered enumeration kind, policy_decision, reparse_tag, strong_identity, allocation_size, end_of_file, number_of_links, and supplied_stream_records
  + [ComparisonAccount] is a fixed array containing every StabilityComparedField exactly once in declaration order
  + [StablePair] preserves profile, reconciliation identity, common entry reference, distinct batch identities, comparison account, and both admitted observations
  + [ReconciliationFault] is one closed code, optional nested side, optional difference field, bounded field name, and bounded reason
  + [source_data] is the two strict nested assembly inputs
  + [derived_projection] is the stable pair or fault
  + [state] is absent
  + [persistence] is absent

& [IdentityDiscipline] keeps every namespace local
  + [natural_request_key] is profile plus reconciliation_identity inside the caller's unstated scope
  + [technical_identity] is unnecessary because the transform is stateless and returns no registry object
  + [entry_reference_identity] is caller syntax shared by two nested batches
  + [batch_identity] is caller syntax scoped to one nested record batch
  + [identity_authority] is the caller for syntax only
  + [identity_stability_window] is this one transform call
  - never: treat any identity as globally unique, authenticated, persistent, or physically sourced

& [ConceptualLogicalPhysicalSeparation] is explicit
  + [conceptual] two caller-designated observations are compared for exact supplied entry-local equality
  + [logical] strict request, independent assembly results, syntax gates, ordered comparison, stable pair, and typed fault
  + [physical] one in-memory safe-Rust transform over owned values and serde JSON
  + [model_independence] later physical producers may construct the nested inputs without changing comparison meaning
  - never: let the physical representation create temporal or provenance truth

& [LifecycleAndTransformOrder] is linear and fail closed
  + [stage_1] decode outer request strictly when using the JSON entry point
  + [stage_2] verify outer profile and nonzero reconciliation identity
  + [stage_3] assemble pre_read independently
  + [stage_4] assemble post_read independently
  + [stage_5] require equal nonzero entry-reference identities
  + [stage_6] require distinct nonzero batch identities
  + [stage_7] compare each closed field in canonical order
  + [stage_8] release one stable pair only after every comparison passes
  + [terminal_fault] any failure stops later stages and releases no pair

& [NestedAssemblyTruthTable] is exhaustive
  + [pre_and_post_pass] proceeds to syntax identity
  + [pre_fails] emits pre_read nested fault and does not assemble post_read
  + [pre_passes_post_fails] emits post_read nested fault and no pair
  + [nested_fault_identity] preserves the existing assembly fault code through a closed side-specific wrapper
  - never: compare raw invalid inputs directly

& [SyntaxIdentityTruthTable] is exhaustive
  + [outer_reconciliation_nonzero] is required
  + [entry_references_nonzero_and_equal] proceeds
  + [entry_reference_difference] rejects before field comparison
  + [batch_identities_nonzero_and_distinct] proceeds
  + [batch_identity_equal] rejects reuse of one declared batch as both roles
  + [meaning] all identities remain caller-owned syntax only

& [ComparisonTruthTable] is exact
  + [all_eight_fields_equal] releases stable pair
  + [kind_differs] emits kind as first difference
  + [policy_decision_differs_after_kind_equal] emits policy_decision
  + [reparse_tag_differs_after_prior_equal] emits reparse_tag
  + [strong_identity_differs_after_prior_equal] emits strong_identity
  + [allocation_size_differs_after_prior_equal] emits allocation_size
  + [end_of_file_differs_after_prior_equal] emits end_of_file
  + [number_of_links_differs_after_prior_equal] emits number_of_links
  + [supplied_stream_records_differs_after_prior_equal] emits supplied_stream_records
  + [comparison_semantics] use exact PartialEq over admitted deterministic value shapes
  - never: reorder, normalize, tolerate, score, or compare only a subset

& [FaultTruthTable] is closed
  + [profile] unknown outer profile
  + [reconciliation_identity] zero caller reconciliation identity
  + [pre_read] nested pre-read assembly fault
  + [post_read] nested post-read assembly fault
  + [entry_reference] unequal admitted entry-reference identities
  + [batch_identity] equal admitted batch identities
  + [difference] first exact field difference
  + [resource] bounded diagnostic or representation limit not covered elsewhere
  + [json] malformed, unknown, omitted, wrong-type, or unknown-variant serialized input
  + [difference_field] is present only for difference
  + [nested_side] is present only for pre_read or post_read

& [StableOutputContract] is inspectable and non-authorizing
  + [profile] is exact outer profile
  + [reconciliation_identity] is exact caller input
  + [entry_reference_identity] is the common admitted syntax token
  + [pre_batch_identity] is exact admitted pre-read batch token
  + [post_batch_identity] is exact admitted post-read batch token
  + [compared_fields] is the exact fixed eight-value ordered array
  + [pre_read] and [post_read] preserve the exact admitted observations
  + [no_boolean_collapse] the output retains the data that justified structural equality
  - never: expose stable together with a fault
  - never: upgrade stable pair to physical temporal evidence

& [ConstraintLedger] is fail closed
  + [C-01] source and manifest remain byte-bound and separate from derived artifacts
  + [C-02] outer profile is exactly cantor-windows-supplied-entry-stability/0.1
  + [C-03] pre_read and post_read are nonoptional strict AssemblyInput values
  + [C-04] current governing supplied-entry assembly signature remains valid
  + [C-05] both nested inputs pass the existing assembly transform independently
  + [C-06] reconciliation identity is nonzero
  + [C-07] entry-reference identities are nonzero and equal
  + [C-08] batch identities are nonzero and distinct
  + [C-09] comparison field set is closed, ordered, and exhaustive for every admitted observation field except batch identity and shared entry-reference identity already handled by syntax gates
  + [C-10] first-difference output is deterministic
  + [C-11] faults release no partial stable pair
  + [C-12] output preserves both observations and fixed comparison account
  + [C-13] no type or field claims actual before, after, elapsed, same handle, same object, path, Windows, completeness, freshness, or trust
  + [C-14] no TopologyEntryObservation, content digest, receipt, or admission output exists
  + [C-15] production imports remain std, serde, and the existing pure assembly module
  + [C-16] Cargo, lockfile, dependency, unsafe, platform, filesystem, process, environment, clock, network, persistence, model, and effect deltas remain zero

& [SubcomponentWeaveTrace] is source grounded
  + [request] originates in InputShape and weaves to strict serde and outer validation tests
  + [nested_assembly] originates in the no-bypass clause and weaves to side-specific nested faults
  + [syntax_identities] originate in SyntaxIdentity and weave to zero, equality, and distinctness tests
  + [comparison_fields] originate in ExactComparison and weave to fixed enum order plus one test per difference
  + [stable_pair] originates in StableOutput and weaves to exact preservation and atomic release tests
