& [SemanticRefinementTrace] is exact
  + [pre_read] means caller-designated left role, not proven earlier physical time
  + [post_read] means caller-designated right role, not proven later physical time
  + [stable] means exact equality of the closed admitted entry-local field set
  + [reconciliation] means deterministic comparison and accounting, not repair, merge, or truth adjudication
  + [batch_distinct] prevents literal role reuse but proves neither separate calls nor order
  + [entry_reference_equal] means syntax equality only
  + [difference] means supplied admitted values differ, not that the underlying file changed

& [ConstraintCheckTrace] is grounded
  + [source] requires independent assembly, strict syntax identity, exact ordered comparison, inspectable stable pair, typed faults, and explicit nonclaims
  + [selection_review] chooses this seam before physical production so race semantics do not hide in unsafe code
  + [assembly] provides public strict input and output types plus one validating transform and prohibits physical claims
  + [topology_formation] requires entry-local pre-read and post-read facts while separately requiring directory and whole-root repetition
  + [data_design] requires explicit identity namespaces, transform order, source-versus-derived distinction, and conceptual-logical-physical separation
  + [framework] requires source preservation, separate explosion, justification, plan, registry, and governing signature evidence

& [ConstraintReapplicationTrace] preserves repairs
  + [repair_1] compare nested assembly inputs only after invoking the existing validator rather than trusting public structs
  + [repair_2] require distinct batch identities but state that distinctness is not order proof
  + [repair_3] compare full policy decision so component, attributes, case, and order key cannot drift invisibly
  + [repair_4] compare raw ordered stream records rather than only derived sorted stream facts
  + [repair_5] preserve both admitted observations instead of reducing evidence to one boolean
  + [unresolved] physical acquisition and actual order remain separate future authority

& [PruningTrace] removes overreach
  + [pruned] a boolean stable input or output without inspectable values
  + [pruned] caller assertions named same_handle, queried, complete, trusted, fresh, or ordered
  + [pruned] clocks, timestamps, durations, or generated identities
  + [pruned] tolerant, subset, unordered, normalized, lexical, probabilistic, or learned comparison
  + [pruned] direct content-digest, path, Git-mode, ordinal, TopologyEntryObservation, receipt, or admission construction
  + [pruned] physical query, buffer, pointer, handle, Win32, filesystem, traversal, and effect behavior
  + [pruned] persistence because the stable pair is returned data rather than durable state

